u\\times v.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the determinant formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u\\times v & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 10 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 7 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}10 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 1\\end{vmatrix}i-\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{vmatrix}j+\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 10 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{vmatrix}k \\\\  & =(10\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 7)i-((-3)\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 4)j+((-3)\\cdot 7-10\\cdot 4)k \\\\  & =(10-28)i-(-3-16)j+(-21-40)k \\\\  & =-18i+19j-61k \\\\  & =⟨-18,19,-61⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060047 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c52df7a-329a-513d-ba90-59439fdf20c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨45, 0, 1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056641} {:answer/id #uuid "9fe22398-ad1d-5641-9ca1-2d178280b598" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨45, 1, 1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056642} {:answer/id #uuid "22d1b2c3-1252-5258-a581-4139af6aa2b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨9,-1, 1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056643} {:answer/id #uuid "281c2db9-0585-56df-8397-d9d5d0c07e0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨45,-1,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056644} {:answer/id #uuid "626cdb03-c38d-59fb-ae90-c0a438b0b03c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - 9,-1,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056645}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6955e160-edc6-5daf-b539-aec04e8f2cc3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186056640}] :question/id #uuid "eee40076-098f-5267-94c9-3c8be76fb995" :question/math-academy-id "q-1408" :question/problem "Let $u = ⟨\\frac{1}{3}, 9, 6⟩$ and $v = ⟨0,-3, 3⟩$. Find $u \\cdot v$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060071 :