905d55d3bce" :question/math-academy-id "q-70401" :question/problem "Find $a + b$ if $a = 7i - 6j$ and $b = 3i + 2j$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060393 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "819bbd77-81fe-5b0c-9709-5c20913178d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2i - 2j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058981} {:answer/id #uuid "a9c53f60-402e-51b4-9ae0-6ebe0157d93b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058982} {:answer/id #uuid "b0f501e7-842b-5916-8760-d05182b0f466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14i + 2j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058983} {:answer/id #uuid "05b0b519-c4c6-5a48-bc7f-81176270be84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058984} {:answer/id #uuid "2e1600f0-3fc1-5dad-bc64-a8c5fa92fbb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14i - 2j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058985}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6e77c6a2-22c0-59a3-b06d-8d99ffe45d98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186058980}] :question/id #uuid "0e61282c-5ba8-52b2-b8ef-94b1e6e60711" :question/math-academy-id "q-70402" :question/problem "Find $2a + b$ if $a = 4i + 2j$ and $b = 6i - 4j$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064038 :question/id #uuid "368cbbae-4eff-5eff-a8f3-d3e8359447a9" :question/math-academy-id "e-364" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int x^2 \\,\\textrm d x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the power rule with $n=2$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\int x^2 \\,\\textrm d x = \\dfrac{x^{2+1}}{2+1} + C = \\dfrac{x^3}{3}+C.\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 3{x}^{2} \\\\ &= {x}^{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064039 :question/id #uuid "818f4fbe-e251-57bd-90ae-b6517c6f2f89" :question/math-academy-id "e-367" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of  $\\sqrt x.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by writing the square root as a rational power, $\\sqrt x= x^{1/2}.$ So, we can apply the power rule with $n=\\dfrac{1}{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{1/2+1}}{(\\frac{1}{2}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3/2}}{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3/2})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}{x}^{3/2-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{1/2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064040 :question/id #uuid "c25e6037-3900-5314-b9a9-262fef07061c" :question/math-academy-id "e-368" :question/problem "Given that $f(x) = \\dfrac 1 {x^3}$ and that $F'(x) = f(x)$, calculate $F(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if $F'(x) = f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{′}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\dfrac 1 {x^3}= x^{-3}.$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-3$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-3+1}}{-3+1}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{-2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{x}^{2}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064068 :question/id #uuid "e2c444fd-31b5-505f-844d-313f9efb7f45" :question/math-academy-id "e-409" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle\\int_0^4 x \\, \\textrm d x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{1+1}}{1+1}{|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{2} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064069 :question/id #uuid "e0bb9783-9d30-5139-a2c0-aae55ea18733" :question/math-academy-id "e-410" :question/problem "Evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int _{1}^2\\dfrac 1 {x^3}\\, \\textrm d x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{1}{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-3+1}}{-3+1}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{-2}}{2}{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}({2}^{-2}-{1}^{-2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{4}-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\left(-\\frac{3}{4}\\right) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064070 :question/id #uuid "77d37915-81e0-5415-8377-a3aae532e1f2" :question/math-academy-id "e-411" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle\\int_1^4\\sqrt x\\, \\textrm d x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the antiderivative and evaluating the difference at the bounds, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}{x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{3/2}{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}({4}^{3/2}-{1}^{3/2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\sqrt{64}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(8-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064554 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd9ded59-ba65-5176-b8f9-b0abbcde8e5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061520} {:answer/id #uuid "06876c28-ebd0-5db2-80b3-e9af69ed8c2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061521} {:answer/id #uuid "1e1c848c-bcad-5a85-903a-9791288e9010" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061522} {:answer/id #uuid "53a354ab-679e-5199-ac84-f449177db3d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061523} {:answer/id #uuid "759d2e84-4518-561f-8c74-506babc880c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06876c28-ebd0-5db2-80b3-e9af69ed8c2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061521} :answer-field/id #uuid "d83860ac-499e-5a75-812f-1da4dee6be22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061519}] :question/id #uuid "9681ab06-ae34-5546-895c-3849a33f13b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-2005" :question/problem "Calculate the integral.\n\n$$\n\\int x\\,\\mathrm{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Apply the sum and constant multiple rules, using the power rule or the standard trigonometric/exponential antiderivative for each term:\n\n$$\n\\int x\\,\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{x^{2}}{2} + C.\n$$\n\nDifferentiate the result to check:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\left(\\frac{x^{2}}{2}+C\\right)=x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064556 :question/answer-fields [{:a